                   QRS  (Quick Replacement String)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------


``     =  QRS indicator
.[n]   =  QRS command extension, reserve [n] spaces for this text.

A few commands MUST be ended with a "@", or you will see incredible things
happening. Note, only needed if said so after command name help.



example
-------------
``USERNAME.30    :will display current users name, and reserve 30 spaces for
                 :the text...

``DOOR STATUS@   :will run the STATUS door found in your
                        {BBSMAINPATH}COMMANDS/SYSCMD     or,
                        {BBSMAINPATH}COMMANDS/BBSCMD

                 :Command is ignored if door is not found, QRS command is cut
                 : out of text, and will not be displayed to user.






                       Commands available
                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                       ------------------

NONSTOP			: Do not check users line length.
			: Suppress the "resume y/n/ns" prompt.

DISPLAY {pt}@		: Display textfile, where {pt} is full path and
                        : filename of text to be displayed.

DOOR {name} {pt}@	: run door {name}, and use parameters {pt} as
			: simulated start from menu prompt with parameters.

PRESSAKEY		: Wait for a keypress, before continue displaying.

USERNAME		: Users name

USERLOC			: Users location

CONFNAME		: Current conference name

USERACCESS		: Users accesslevel

TIME			: A current time text, example -> 12:00

DATE			: A current date text, example -> 12-Jan-95

DL_BYTE			: Download bytes (conference)

UL_BYTE			: Upload bytes   (conference)

DL_FILE			: Download files (conference)

UL_FILE			: Upload files   (conference)

DL_LIMIT		: Daily download byte limit (conference)

DL_TODAY		: Downloaded bytes today  (conference)

USERNO			: User slotnumber

PHONE_INTCODE		: International dialingcode

VOICEPHONE		: Users voice number

DATAPHONE		: Users Data/Fax number

CELLUARPHONE		: Users celluar/mobile phone number

USERTYPE		: Usertype

RATIO			: Users ratio (conference)

NODE			: Node number

TIMELIMIT		: Daily timelimit

TIMEUSED		: Time used this day

TIMEALL			: Time used on system since first time on.

CHATLIMIT		: Chat limit daily

CHATUSED		: Chat time used today

CHATALL			: Chattime used on system since first time on.

MSGPOST			: Messages posted since first logon.

FIRST			: Date & time string showing first logon. 

LAST			: Last call to system.

BIRTH			: Users birthday

CALLS			: Calls made to system since first time on.

CALLSTODAY		: Calls made to system this day

CPSTOPU			: CPS top rate on uploaded files.

CPSTOPD			: CPS top rate on downloaded files.

BAUDRATE		: Users connected baudrate

SCREENLINES		: Users choosen number of lines to view.

SCREENWIDTH		: Users choosen width of a line.

SCREENCLEAR		: Users choice of sending screenclearing codes.

CHATOLM			: Available for chat/olm

RATIOTYPE		: Users ratio type

PROTOCOL		: Users selected protocol.


